'''G1 Climax 2026 Day 19''' was the nineteenth and final block-stage show of the [[G1 Climax 2026]] tournament produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on October 10, 2026 at the Toyozawa Municipal Gymnasium in [[Toyozawa]]. The show was headlined by the first playoff match in G1 history — [[Taumafa Vaiahi|Taumafa]] against [[Takagi Yuto]] for the [[G1 Climax 2026|Block B]] championship, after both men finished the nine-round block stage level on 14 points.

== Background ==

Taumafa and Takagi finished the block stage tied at 7-2 with 14 points each. Takagi held the head-to-head — the Dragon lariat in Tsuda on October 5 — but G1 regulations decide a first-place tie by playoff match, not tiebreaker. The Toyozawa Municipal Gymnasium, which had hosted Day 18 the previous night, was held over for the playoff; the remaining tickets sold out within the hour.

