== Match details ==

* '''Match 1: Seigigun (Ono & Iwata) def. Cannon Club (Tanaka & Viggo).''' The young lions' opener — Ono, the block's adopted son, and Iwata against the Bulldog and El Phantasma. Tanaka's brawling kept the Cannon Club in it, but the Seigigun's speed told on the junior tag champion: Iwata's running knee and the Iwata Cutter at 9:41 pinned Viggo clean. '''Crowd:''' '''ONO''' chants throughout. POP for the Cutter.
* '''Match 2: Seigigun (Kuroki & Ishida) def. CHAOS (Fujinami & Reyes).''' The building came for the playoff and got the Ishida Lock first. Kuroki and Reyes renewed their strong-style thread from the block — the forearms, the Cobra Twist teased and escaped — before Ishida took Fujinami to the mat and never gave him back. The Ishida Lock at 14:22, center of the ring: the sixth submission of the television champion's tour. '''Crowd:''' '''ISHIDA''' chants — the loudest of the undercard. Standing ovation on the walk-out.
* '''Match 3: KAZUKI & Maeda def. Jusuf & Diallo.''' The Kuroshio reunion — KAZUKI and Ryohei Maeda teaming for the first time since the 2017 excursion — and Jusuf Muntasir wanted no part of it. The truth-teller wrestled eight minutes of contemptuous mat-work, then refused Diallo's tag, stepped off the apron, and walked out, leaving the Hammer to the reunion: Maeda's Speed Star Press set the table, KAZUKI's Twin Star Press ended it at 16:38. After the bell the two of them stood arms crossed, facing the crowd — the old pose — and walked out through separate exits. '''Crowd:''' ERUPTION at the pose. '''KUROSHIO''' chants. BOOS for Jusuf's walk-out.
* '''Block B playoff: Taumafa def. Takagi.''' The Dragon and the giant, one more time, for everything. Takagi had won Tsuda with one move, so Taumafa's answer was to take the move away: ten minutes of arm and shoulder work, the Samoan drop on the apron, the hip attack that sent the Dragon into the barricade. Takagi's comeback was the tournament's bravest — the elbow exchanges, the corner charge, the near fall off the diving shoulder at 22. And then the moment the building will keep: the Dragon lariat connected flush at 24:40 — and Taumafa kicked out at 2.9, the first man to survive the move all tournament. The second lariat never landed. Taumafa caught the arm, spun him in — Samoan driver — one, two, three at 26:52. Taumafa wins Block B, and the family goes to the Aizawa Dome. '''Crowd:''' '''TAUMAFA''' chants throughout. ERUPTION at the kickout. STANDING OVATION at the bell — and '''TAKAGI''' chants on the Dragon's walk-out, the crowd's verdict on both men.

