''Playoff (October 10, Toyozawa): Taumafa def. Takagi. Taumafa wins Block B and advances to the G1 Final against Block A winner [[Marcus Vance]].''

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The giant answers Tsuda.''' Takagi's Dragon lariat was the only clean loss of Taumafa's tournament — and in the playoff the giant survived it, caught the second one, and drove the Dragon into the Toyozawa canvas. The Final is set: [[Marcus Vance|Marcus "The Drill" Vance]] vs. Taumafa, October 18, Aizawa Dome. The winner challenges [[Leoni Masua]] at Wrestling Summit.
* '''The Ishida Lock decided Block B without being in the match.''' The playoff existed only because Ishida submitted Takagi on Day 8 — the block's best story shaped its ending. The television champion submitted Fujinami on the undercard for his sixth of the tour, and the building chanted his name during the playoff entrances.
* '''The Kuroshio reunion.''' KAZUKI and Maeda, arms crossed, separate exits — nine years gone in one pose. And Jusuf Muntasir walked out on his own partner rather than share a ring with it.
* '''Vance watches.''' The perfect block now has its opponent: the Workhorse against the giant, silence against ceremony, the Drill Driver against the Samoan driver. Eight days.

